        "subject": "LU-20422 llite: use lockless inode_state_read_once",
        "message": "LU-20422 llite: use lockless inode_state_read_once\n\nOn v6.18+, inode_state_read() asserts i_lock is held via\nlockdep_assert_held(). Lustre's call sites read i_state locklessly\n(e.g. the I_NEW check in ll_iget() after iget5_locked()), so the\nassertion trips a WARN). Use the lockless inode_state_read_once()\nvariant instead, matching the original bare i_state reads.\n\nFixes: 20527615330e (\"LU-19837 build: Compatibility updates for kernel v6.19\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ie9a36f3e54a2c1f7fccda0a4cabcf20fa5d692da\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/66823\nReviewed-by: James Simmons <jsimmons@infradead.org>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Shaun Tancheff <shaun.tancheff@hpe.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
